<h1>🧬 DNA Spiral — English Worksheet</h1>
<p><strong>Topic:</strong> Lists and <code>%</code> make a spiral · <strong>Course:</strong> 3D Coordinates · <strong>Level:</strong> Extension · <strong>Time:</strong> about 40 minutes</p>
<p><span class="timing">Type <code>del</code> before every <code>run</code>. This build is 30 tall.</span></p>
<p>Every <code>???</code> is one short thing for you to work out. There are no answers on this sheet.</p>
<hr />
<h2>1 · Eight spots 📍</h2>
<p>Two lists hold eight places around a circle.</p>
<pre><code class="language-python">XS = [ 6, 4, 0, -4, -6, -4,  0,  4]
ZS = [ 0, 4, 6,  4,  0, -4, -6, -4]
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Spot 0 is <code>XS[0]</code>, <code>ZS[0]</code>. Write it.</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>Write spot 2 and spot 5.</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>The centre is (8, 8). Spot 0 lands at x = 8 + 6 = 14. Where does spot 4 land?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<div class="check"><span class="lab">Got it right if</span> spot 0 and spot 4 are on opposite sides of the centre.</div>

<hr />
<h2>2 · The <code>%</code> sign 🔁</h2>
<p><code>%</code> gives the <strong>remainder</strong> after dividing.</p>
<p><strong>Fill this in.</strong></p>
<table class="tr">
<tr><th>i</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>7</th><th>8</th><th>9</th><th>15</th><th>16</th></tr>
<tr><th>i % 8</th><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr>
</table>

<p><strong>What is the biggest number <code>i % 8</code> can ever be?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<div class="mini-q">Why this matters.</div>

<p><strong>Your lists only have 8 spots. <code>i</code> counts to 23. Explain what <code>%</code> is doing for you.</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<hr />
<h2>3 · The other strand ↔️</h2>
<pre><code class="language-python">k = i % 8
j = (k + 4) % 8
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Fill this in.</strong></p>
<table class="tr">
<tr><th>k</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th><th>5</th><th>6</th><th>7</th></tr>
<tr><th>j</th><td>4</td><td>5</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr>
</table>

<p><strong>Why is there a second <code>% 8</code> on the <code>j</code> line? What goes wrong without it?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<div class="check"><span class="lab">Got it right if</span> every j is between 0 and 7.</div>

<hr />
<h2>4 · Build it 🧬</h2>
<div class="tpl">Template</div>

<pre><code class="language-python">XS = [6, 4, 0, -4, -6, -4, 0, 4]
ZS = [0, 4, 6, 4, 0, -4, -6, -4]

def on_chat():
    for i in range(0, 24):
        k = i % 8
        j = (??? + ???) % ???
        ax = 8 + XS[k]
        az = 8 + ZS[k]
        bx = 8 + XS[???]
        bz = 8 + ZS[???]
        blocks.fill(GOLD_BLOCK,
            pos(ax, ???, az), pos(ax + 1, ???, az + 1), REPLACE)
        blocks.fill(EMERALD_BLOCK,
            pos(bx, ???, bz), pos(bx + 1, ???, bz + 1), REPLACE)
player.on_chat(&quot;dna&quot;, on_chat)
</code></pre>
<div class="mini-q">The `y` blanks are all the same thing.</div>

<p><strong>Which variable makes it climb?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<div class="check"><span class="lab">Works when</span> two coloured strands wind around each other, and they are never on the same side.</div>

<div class="stuck"><span class="lab">It is a straight tower?</span>
Your `y` is a fixed number instead of a variable. It must change every turn.</div>

<div class="stuck"><span class="lab">Both strands in the same place?</span>
Check the `j` line. `(k + 4)` not `(k + 8)`.</div>

<hr />
<h2>5 · Add the bars 🪜</h2>
<p>Real DNA has rungs joining the two strands.</p>
<div class="tpl">Template · inside the loop</div>

<pre><code class="language-python">        if i % ??? == 0:
            blocks.fill(QUARTZ_BLOCK,
                pos(ax, i, az), pos(bx, i, bz), REPLACE)
</code></pre>
<p><strong>24 steps. You want 6 bars. What number goes in the blank?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<div class="check"><span class="lab">Works when</span> you can count your bars and get the number you planned.</div>

<hr />
<h2>6 · Show Your Work 📸🎥</h2>
<p>Record <strong>one video</strong>, one take, no stopping. A phone is fine. Show these in order:</p>
<blockquote>
<ol>
<li>Type <code>del</code>, then <code>dna</code>. Walk all the way round it.</li>
<li>Show your two lists and say what one spot means.</li>
<li>Show the <code>k</code> line and explain <code>%</code> in your own words.</li>
<li>Show the <code>j</code> line and say why it is always the opposite side.</li>
<li>Show your bars and say how you chose the number.</li>
</ol>
</blockquote>
<p>Try to use these words: <strong>list</strong>, <strong>remainder</strong>, <strong>opposite</strong>, <strong>loop</strong>, <strong>climb</strong>.</p>
<p><strong>Plan what you will say before you record.</strong></p>
